From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shphadnis <134159681+shphadnis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:53:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] spectro: bump golang.org/x deps and spdystream for PVM-1439
 CVEs

govulncheck flagged reachable advisories in golang.org/x/net
(GO-2026-5026, -6603, -6610, -6611, -6612, -6617), golang.org/x/crypto
(GO-2026-5013, -5016..-5020, -6354, -6355), golang.org/x/text
(GO-2026-5970) and github.com/moby/spdystream (GO-2026-4958).

Root module and the two nested modules that ship in images
(cmd/kubectl-mtv, cmd/vsphere-copy-offload-populator):
  golang.org/x/net    v0.53.0 -> v0.60.0
  golang.org/x/crypto v0.50.0 -> v0.57.0
  golang.org/x/text   v0.36.0 -> v0.42.0
  github.com/moby/spdystream v0.5.0 -> v0.5.1 (root only)
plus the x/sys, x/term, x/sync, x/mod, x/tools versions those require.

x/net >= v0.59.0 and x/crypto >= v0.56.0 declare go 1.26, so the go
directive moves 1.25.0 -> 1.26.0. godebug default=go1.25 keeps the Go
1.25 runtime defaults: without it urlstrictcolons=1 and friends switch
on, which broke the Vantara client tests. Images already build with Go
1.26.10, so the stdlib advisories in the ticket are closed by the
toolchain.

The nested modules' vendored copy of github.com/kubev2v/forklift (via
replace ../../) is left as it was; re-vendoring it would pull the fork's
API changes into kubectl-mtv and the copy-offload populator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
